{
  "anomaly_detected": true,
  "confidence": 0.92,
  "anomalies": [
    {
      "category": "wrong_value",
      "components": [
        "R29",
        "U7"
      ],
      "pins": [
        "R29.1",
        "R29.2",
        "U7.17"
      ],
      "nets": [
        "/VREF_{NB}",
        "GND"
      ],
      "observed": "R29 is the bottom VREF divider resistor for U7. Its schematic value field is \"10M7\" and the SPICE deck models it as 10.7Meg, but the component's own library part, description, and PN identify it as 10.7 kΩ. The corresponding resistors for U5 and U6, R25 and R27, are explicitly 10k7. This makes the U7 VREF node effectively see 10.7 MΩ to ground instead of 10.7 kΩ.",
      "expected": "R29 should be 10.7 kΩ, matching R25/R27 and the 14 kΩ top resistor R28, so U7's VREF divider sets approximately the same reference voltage as U5 and U6 (about 2.0 V from the 5 VOUT rail).",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "source": "netlist",
          "quote": "(comp (ref \"R29\")\n      (value \"10M7\")"
        },
        {
          "source": "netlist",
          "quote": "(description \"10.7 kOhms ±1% 0.125W, 1/8W Chip Resistor 0805 (2012 Metric) Moisture Resistant Thick Film\")"
        },
        {
          "source": "netlist",
          "quote": "(field (name \"PN\") \"RC0805FR-0710K7L\")"
        },
        {
          "source": "spice",
          "quote": "R29 0 /VREFNB 10.7Meg"
        },
        {
          "source": "netlist",
          "quote": "(comp (ref \"R25\")\n      (value \"10k7\")"
        },
        {
          "source": "spec",
          "quote": "VREF-setting resistors R24–R29"
        }
      ],
      "impact": "U7's current reference would be pulled to nearly 5 V instead of the intended ~2 V, causing the Nutrient-B stepper driver to command a much higher motor current than the other dosing pumps. This can overdrive the pump, overheat the driver, or damage the dosing hardware.",
      "confidence": 0.92
    }
  ],
  "summary": "The design files otherwise match the described architecture, but R29 is clearly inconsistent: its value/SPICE model is 10.7 MΩ while its part metadata and the parallel U5/U6 dividers require 10.7 kΩ. This is a high-confidence wrong-value anomaly affecting the U7 TMC2209 current reference."
}

